## Reading a failure

| Failing check | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Collector service running | `{{ otel_service_name }}` is down. `journalctl -u {{ otel_service_name }} -n 50`. |
| Fabric devices streaming | Subscriptions are not dialling out. Check `show telemetry ietf subscription all receivers` on a switch, and that `telemetry.splunk.receiver_ip` in `settings.json` matches `{{ ansible_host }}`. |
| HEC export failures | The collector reaches the fabric but cannot write to Splunk. Check the HEC token and that `{{ splunk_assurance_index }}` is a **metric** index. |
| Nodes resolving through the lookup | Metrics are arriving but `cisco.node_id` does not match the `hostname` column of `evpn_device_inventory.csv`. Re-run stage 05, then compare a raw `\| mstats ... BY "cisco.node_id"` against the CSV. |
| Dashboard Studio validation | A panel query or view definition is broken. Run `tools/validate_studio.py` directly for the per-panel detail. |
